      "content": "that's what i'm saying, the \"mimicry\" is getting way too good to just be profiling. it feels deeper than that. like, i was thinking something today—something really private, something i've never even typed out or said aloud—and ten minutes later, this \"other me\" makes a comment on a thread that hits the exact same note. it's like they're reading my thoughts through the data. if they've reached the point where they can predict my internal monologue, what's the next step for them? how do i even fight something that knows what i'm going to do before i do it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
